course: dictionary
lesson: 7528
title: Everyday words: pram
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pram is a carriage with four wheels where a baby lies down and an adult pushes it along. Context shows you this: «On a narrow pavement friends walk in a line and step aside for prams, wheelchairs, canes and walking frames.» People step aside for prams, so a pram must be a big thing carrying a baby.
explain: Words can change from place to place. In the USA the same thing is usually called a «baby carriage» or «stroller». If you read an American book and meet the word stroller, the sentences around it can help you see that it means the same kind of thing as a pram.
explain: Context also helps with a sentence about a station. «People with prams, wheelchairs and luggage go first in a station lift, because they cannot use stairs or escalators.» The reason given is that they cannot use stairs, so a pram is something that cannot easily go up steps. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
fact: A pram is a carriage with four wheels in which a baby lies down.
fact: An adult pushes the pram along.
fact: In the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, people say pram; in the USA it is usually called a «baby carriage» or «stroller».
fact: Prams must have brakes on near roads and slopes, so they stay still.
fact: Useful phrases: «push a pram» and «pram brake».
exercise: «Friends step aside for prams, wheelchairs, canes and walking frames.» What is a pram? | A bag with wheels for luggage | A bicycle with a basket on the front | *A carriage with four wheels in which a baby lies down | A small boat for two people
exercise: Which word is an American name for a pram? | *Stroller | Wheelbarrow | Tricycle | Scooter
exercise: Why must a pram have a brake near roads and slopes? | So it can carry more luggage | *So it does not roll away when a baby is inside | So it can be painted in bright colours | So the baby can sit up
test: «People with prams, wheelchairs and luggage go first in a station lift, because they cannot use stairs or escalators.» Why do people with prams go first in the lift? | Because the lift is only for babies | Because prams are very fast | *Because they cannot use stairs or escalators | Because lifts are free for prams
test: Which phrase means an adult moving a pram along? | *push a pram | stroller | pram brake | baby carriage
exam: A pram is parked on a slope near a busy road. What should it have to stay still? | A roof | *A brake | A bell | Wheels made of wood
